  data: {
    LLM: "Lead a Manille (10) of a non-trump suit early - it will likely 'go round' (laten rondgoan) as no one can beat it without trumping. Save your trumps for when you need to win crucial tricks.\n\nCreate voids (renoang) by discarding your only card of a suit on a trick your partner is winning. This allows you to trump when that suit is led. Avoid being stuck with an 'blooten aas' (lone Ace) - an Ace without other cards of that suit, which is vulnerable to being trumped.\n\nCount cards carefully - this is essential in Manillen. Track which Manilles and Aces have been played. If you know all trumps are gone, your plain suit cards become more valuable. Use 'vet'n' (fattening) - playing high value cards on your partner's winning trick to capture those points safely.",
    Player: "Lead a Manille (10) of a non-trump suit early - it will likely 'go round' (laten rondgoan) as no one can beat it without trumping. Save your trumps for when you need to win crucial tricks.\n\nCreate voids (renoang) by discarding your only card of a suit on a trick your partner is winning. This allows you to trump when that suit is led. Avoid being stuck with an 'blooten aas' (lone Ace) - an Ace without other cards of that suit, which is vulnerable to being trumped.\n\nCount cards carefully - this is essential in Manillen. Track which Manilles and Aces have been played. If you know all trumps are gone, your plain suit cards become more valuable. Use 'vet'n' (fattening) - playing high value cards on your partner's winning trick to capture those points safely.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
